{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Documentation will be split into two distinct tracks: v0.6 for stable operational platforms and v1.0 for development features, using a static site generator.",
    "The Node SDK will be developed in TypeScript to provide strong typing and better developer experience for application developers.",
    "Channel configuration transactions will follow the standard configuration block structure, extending the API mentioned in FAB-687.",
    "Peer upgrades will leverage the existing lifecycle chaincode (LCCC) and system chaincode (SCC) mechanisms to ensure data persistence.",
    "Ledger refactoring will decouple unit tests from MSP security dependencies by using mock implementations."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has prior experience with Hyperledger Fabric, Go, and Node.js.",
    "Existing CI/CD pipelines and testing frameworks are already in place and do not need to be built from scratch.",
    "The referenced Gerrit changes (1795, 2581) are accessible and provide a baseline for the required modifications.",
    "Visual aids and scripts for U5 will be created using standard diagramming tools and shell scripts.",
    "The estimate covers only development effort (design, coding, testing, documentation) and excludes project management and operational deployment."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and Onboarding",
      "activity_description": "Create getting started guides for new visitors, and maintain up-to-date documentation separating v0.6 (stable) and v1.0 (development) tracks. (U1, U6)",
      "most_likely_effort": 45
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Channel Configuration Transaction",
      "activity_description": "Implement and document the new-channel configuration transaction structure and API to allow peers to create channels for private transactions. (U2)",
      "most_likely_effort": 55
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Peer Upgrade and Lifecycle Chaincode",
      "activity_description": "Implement peer upgrade capabilities without data loss using lifecycle chaincode, and support applying patches/fixes via SCC for protocol changes. (U3)",
      "most_likely_effort": 75
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Ledger Code and Test Refactoring",
      "activity_description": "Refactor ledger code and tests to remove old block structure usage, and remove explicit dependency of ledger unit tests on MSP security related components. (U4)",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Architecture Demos and Visual Aids",
      "activity_description": "Create visual aids, diagrams, and demonstration scripts to explain the present architecture and behavior of Fabric v1.0 to collaborators and customers. (U5)",
      "most_likely_effort": 25
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Chaincode Invocation Sanity Check",
      "activity_description": "Implement sanity checks to ensure that only LCCC or normal chaincodes can be invoked, rejecting any other invalid invocation types. (U7)",
      "most_likely_effort": 15
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Node SDK Development",
      "activity_description": "Develop the Node SDK to allow application developers to build NodeJS applications that interact with the blockchain. (U8)",
      "most_likely_effort": 90
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Integration and System Testing",
      "activity_description": "Integrate all components, perform end-to-end testing, and ensure all user stories meet acceptance criteria.",
      "most_likely_effort": 35
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 380
  }
}
```

